[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Unscrew the sun blind retaining bolt.</p><p>2. Move the sun visor slightly.</p><p>3. Disconnect the electrical connections.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Driver&#x27;s sun blind light</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024097\">G31</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Passenger sun blind light</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024099\">G32</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005493.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>1. Take off the courtesy light cover if necessary.</p><p>2. Remove the bulb (press-fitted).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005494.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the sun visor is\nundamaged.</p><p>If removed, fit the bulb  and fit the courtesy\nlight  cover.</p><p>Connect the electrical connection</p><p>Position the sun visor and fix it using\nthe bolts.</p><p>Check that the sun visor works smoothly\nand the courtesy lights are operational.</p>"]]